From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: server: a thread the user's process agent cannot reach fails its suspend instead of pending forever

In a shared prefix the machine's server runs as SYSTEM and stops an ordinary
user's thread (SuspendThread + GetThreadContext, the first thing every .NET
garbage collection does) by signalling it through that user's sg-procagent
(0021). When the agent was not there or did not answer, stop_thread's signal
never went out, the thread's context stayed STATUS_PENDING and whoever waited
for it waited forever: MSBuild and every other .NET program hung at its next
collection (Visual Studio 2022 in the harness, whose user had no agent).

stop_thread now fails that context at once, as for a thread that died
(STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, waiters woken) and drops it, so the next suspend tries
the agent again; get_thread_context and set_thread_context report
ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED for it instead of tripping the self-thread assertion. Only
for a thread signalled through an agent (sg_thread_signal_delegated): nothing
else changes, and no other way to reach the thread is tried -- no signal from
another user, no new channel. The agent's 10 s socket timeout bounds a hung
agent.

sg-session 0.1.0-264 restarts a dead agent (sg_procagent_supervise); this is
the safety net. Wine Mono needs its own half (mono-0016): a blocking thread
whose preemptive suspend failed counts as suspended, rather than being put
back to RUNNING.

Gate: test/agentgone-gate.sh. Mutant: SG_MUTANT_UNREACHABLE_SUSPEND_PENDS.

--- a/server/thread.c
+++ b/server/thread.c
@@ -687,7 +687,23 @@
     if (thread->context) return;  /* already suspended, no need for a signal */
     if (!(thread->context = create_thread_context( thread ))) return;
     /* can't stop a thread while initialisation is in progress */
-    if (is_process_init_done(thread->process)) send_thread_signal( thread, SIGUSR1 );
+    if (!is_process_init_done(thread->process)) return;
+    if (!send_thread_signal( thread, SIGUSR1 ) && sg_thread_signal_delegated( thread ))
+    {
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_UNREACHABLE_SUSPEND_PENDS
+        /* Stained Glass OS: another user's thread, signalled through that user's
+         * process agent (wine-sg 0021), and the agent is not there or did not
+         * answer. The thread will never reach its suspend point, so nothing would
+         * ever fill this context: whoever waits for it (GetThreadContext after
+         * SuspendThread -- Mono's garbage collector) waited forever. Fail it now,
+         * as for a thread that died; the next suspend tries the agent again. No
+         * other way to reach the thread is tried: the agent is the only one. */
+        thread->context->status = STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED;
+        wake_up( &thread->context->obj, 0 );
+        release_object( thread->context );
+        thread->context = NULL;
+#endif
+    }
 }
 
